## 1. Cycles analysis, with computation ([cycle_analysis.py](/home/mdp/muse-work/cp23-redirect/cycle_analysis.py))

[EXACT COMPUTATION] I re-verified A1, the closed form `B_w = Σ_{odd j} 3^{suf_j}·2^j`, `B_w` odd, `B_w ≢ 0 mod 3` for all odd `h < 2^m`, `m ≤ 8`, and A3 (endpoint collision ⟺ `B_w ≡ B_w' mod 3^k`) on all within-stratum pairs, `m ≤ 8`.

[PROOF] From A1, a shortcut-map cycle of length `m` and weight `k` satisfies `x = B_w/D` with `D = 2^m − 3^k`, so `D > 0`, `D | B_w`, and the quotient's length-m word must equal `w` (self-consistency, strictly stronger than divisibility).

[PROOF] `gcd(D,6) = 1` always (`D` is odd; `D ≡ (−1)^m ≢ 0 mod 3`). A2 is 2-adic and A3 is 3-adic; the cycle divisor lives on disjoint prime support. That structural mismatch needs no computation.

[EXACT COMPUTATION] Word-enumeration scan for `m ≤ 12` and `m ∈ {14,16,18,20}`: the only `D`-divisible words are trivial-cycle (`x=1`) repetitions; zero nontrivial cycles. (Mechanism demo only — never a bound.)

[EXACT COMPUTATION] On small-`D` strata, `D`-divisibility runs at/below chance — `(8,5)`: 0/35 vs `1/13`; `(10,6)`: 0/126 vs `1/295`; `(13,8)`: 0/792 vs `1/1631` — and conditioning on A3 class never enriches it (`cond_max = 0` throughout at `n ≥ 6`). Finite tables: consistent with independence, proves nothing.

[PROOF] The 3n−1 map has affine form `(3^k·h − B_w)/2^m` with the same `B_w` (signs flip, magnitudes identical), so its cycles live at `D < 0`. Any future `B_w`-based cycle attack must be sign-sensitive; any ±`D`-symmetric argument is dead on arrival with 3n−1 as witness.

[JUDGEMENT] Verdict: A1+A3 reformulate cycles but exclude nothing. The counting view reproduces the classical doorway (`D|B_w` forces `m/k ≈ log₂3`), but the missing engine — lower bounds for `|2^m − 3^k|` — belongs to Diophantine approximation, which this programme does not own. Honest play: timeboxed lemma hunt aimed below the literature, with a pre-registered kill.

